message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Classical Appearances of pi_g: A Geometric Substitution Note"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Baker
    given-names: Wayne
date-released: 2026-11-10
version: preprint-v1
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24107857
repository-code: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/classical-appearances-of-pi-g"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24107857"
abstract: >-
  An expository note recording representative classical formulae in which pi
  is rewritten as the geometric limiting constant pi_g after the identity
  pi_g=pi has been established. The distinction between the exact completed
  limit and finite approximants is emphasized, with a polygonal N-series and
  Gaussian-normalization illustration.
keywords:
  - pi_g
  - geometric pi
  - geometric substitution
  - N-series
  - Gaussian integral
  - polygonal approximation
  - classical analysis
